      "id": "chord-quality-by-ear",
      "title": "Chord Quality by Ear",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** ear-training | **Difficulty:** 4/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Identifying major, minor, diminished, and seventh chords by ear accelerates session backup and transcription."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "triad-quality",
      "title": "Triad quality",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Major: bright, stable. Minor: darker, melancholic. Diminished: tense, unstable. Augmented: dreamy, unresolved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "seventh-chords",
      "title": "Seventh chords",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Dominant 7th: bluesy tension, wants to resolve. Major 7th: jazzy, sophisticated. Minor 7th: mellow, modal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bass-note",
      "title": "Bass note",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Same chord quality sounds different with different bass — train ear to hear root vs inversion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "progressions",
      "title": "Progressions",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "I–IV–V–I loop — recognise by bass movement and overall colour shift. ii–V–I in jazz."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
